WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.646
Hi, I am Professor Vector. Today: what is a fraction?

2
00:00:05.706 --> 00:00:12.671
A fraction is a fair share of one whole. Here is one whole bar.

3
00:00:12.731 --> 00:00:19.694
Cut it into four equal parts. Each part is one quarter of the bar.

4
00:00:19.754 --> 00:00:29.940
The bottom number of a fraction tells how many equal parts the whole is cut into. Here, four.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.126
The top number tells how many parts we take. Shade three parts: that is three quarters.

6
00:00:38.186 --> 00:00:45.580
The parts must be equal. These pieces are different sizes, so they are not quarters.

7
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:52.174
Same whole, more parts, smaller parts. One eighth is smaller than one quarter.

8
00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:58.767
Two quarters cover the same as one half. Two quarters equals one half.

9
00:00:58.827 --> 00:01:07.880
Fractions of an amount: what is one quarter of twelve bolts? Share them into four equal groups.

10
00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:14.903
One group out of four has three bolts. One quarter of twelve is three.

11
00:01:14.963 --> 00:01:20.693
Now try it yourself. Fraction bars are waiting in your lesson.
